#

assertion  XSH.wctrans.001
anchor     functions/wctrans.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wctrans.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       wctrans() returns a non-zero value for the names tolower and
           toupper.
test       t/001-standard-names.c

assertion  XSH.wctrans.002
anchor     functions/wctrans.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/wctrans.html#ERRORS
class      required
says       wctrans() returns 0 for names that are no mapping in the POSIX
           locale: the empty string, "no such map", "toupper " and "to upper";
           errno is left at 0 or set to EINVAL.
test       t/002-unknown-names.c

assertion  XSH.wctrans.003
anchor     functions/wctrans.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wctrans.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       The handle for toupper maps a to A and the handle for tolower maps
           A to a under towctrans() in the locale it was obtained in.
test       t/003-handle-usable.c

assertion  XSH.wctrans.004
anchor     functions/wctrans.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wctrans.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale the names tolower and toupper also give non-zero
           handles.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale.
test       t/004-utf8-names.c
